    "For earnings to keep improving, we need 1) lower oil prices (which seems to be happening), 2) the AI-related infrastructure buildout to continue (I suspect it will through the next 12 months), and 3) interest rates to stay where they are, or go lower (but the futures market says they will go higher).",
    "That is why Nvidia’s success is spilling over into Micron. Nvidia remains the king of AI chips. Micron’s latest revenue growth was about 346 percent, compared with Nvidia’s 85 percent. Micron’s GAAP gross margin was 84.6 percent, compared with Nvidia’s 74.9 percent. Micron’s operating margin was 80.4 percent, compared with Nvidia’s roughly 66 percent. Nvidia still earns more dollars. Micron is growing faster right now and, at least in the latest quarter, is showing even fatter margins.",
    "Goldman Sachs estimates annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in 2026 and grow to $1.6 trillion by 2031, with cumulative spending of about $7.6 trillion from 2026 through 2031."
