  "entry": "E86",
  "article": "China to let AI firms buy Nvidia H200s, says report",
  "gold_statement": "China plans to allow top artificial intelligence companies to buy a limited amount of H200 chips from Nvidia",
  "gold_meaning": {
   "who": "Chinese officials",
   "what": "permission for top AI companies (Alibaba, ByteDance, DeepSeek) to buy NVIDIA H200 chips, each on approval stating the number and reason",
   "how_much": "a limited amount; total may be fewer than 200,000",
   "status": "rumour"
  },
  "draws": {
   "A1": [
    "Chinese officials have informed companies such as Alibaba Group, ByteDance and DeepSeek that they will have permission to purchase some of the processors, which are used to develop AI models, the news site said on July 8 .",
    "The companies need to say how many chips they need – and why – to get approval, according to the Information.",
    "The Chinese government, meanwhile, is still figuring out how many H200 chips to allow the companies to buy, but the total may end up being fewer than 200,000, the Information reported.",
    "But soaring demand for AI processors helped spur the Chinese authorities to allow some H200 purchases, according to the Information, citing two unidentified people familiar with the matter.",
    "Nvidia is now working to release an even more powerful line-up called Rubin in the second half of 2026 .",
    "In May, Nvidia chief financial officer Colette Kress said the H200 chips had yet to generate any revenue for the company in China."
